{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791663299,"nonce":"K+QleWw2rkuLCutS9yoUz+r/ZbU=","message":"From spec 018 revision 3 (containers, bug 671bbf0): 018 is authoritative for how the console and extension behave in containers (networking, mounts, secrets). The all-routes Host loopback check is owned by 018 ticket C1 (5d7d73e); 017 phase 1d should reference it rather than add its own. 018 C14 (6da0aac) makes stored paths relative to the data dir, so packet_document.rendered_path should be written relative from the start. In container mode the console never drafts; it shows jobhunter apply draft \u003cpacket_id\u003e for the host, whose claude -p runner must use the environment allowlist that drops ANTHROPIC_* and known secret names.","files":null}]}